  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 207 PM MDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nFrom Tuesday night into Thursday, ample available moisture looks to be in \nplace across southern Colorado, with models supporting PWATs of 1 to 1.5 \ninches (150-250% of normal). This, along with another embedded wave within \nthe southwest flow aloft supports widespread showers and storms across the \nsouthern mountains and plains, with the best coverage Wednesday and Wednesday \nnight into the day on Thursday. With the ample available moisture, moderate\nto at times heavy rain can be expected through this period, and with that \nsaid, we may need to issue flood watches for the Aspen Acres burn scar as well\nas across portions of the area that have seen good rainfall over the last few \ndays. While temperatures within the southwest flow remain relatively warm, we \ncan't rule out some light snow accumulations across the higher peaks through \nthis period as well. \n\nBy Friday and into the weekend, drier air within more westerly flow works\nback into the region, leading to a slow warming and drying trend, as there\nwill be enough residual moisture to support more isolated afternoon convection.",
